From c0780a35241d67ba93982dfad37984b2a7aaf209 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 10:35:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: cap VSC pipe width at 2 bins on A22X

A legacy-webOS KGSL capture of the same draws (diag_binning) shows the
proprietary driver drives the a220 hardware binner with plain DRAW_INDX
(no binning pass) and VSC pipes that span at most 2 bins in X (W<=2),
e.g. PIPE_CONFIG 0x01200000/0x01100400/...  freedreno's generic pipe
assignment instead grows tiles-per-pipe in X until the grid fits the 8
pipes, which for >8-bin grids makes a pipe span a whole row (W = nbins_x
= 3 or 4).  The a220 binner mis-routes primitives for such wide pipes,
so its auto-generated visibility stream is garbage -> tile corruption
and a 3D back-end wedge on heavy scenes (glmark desktop blur).

Cap tiles-per-pipe-X at 2 for A22X (only growing tiles-per-pipe-Y if a
tall grid otherwise exceeds the 8 pipes).  With W<=2 the existing
A2XX_VSC_PIPE_CONFIG encoding emits exactly the captured KGSL words
(a pipe at (0,0) with w=2 -> 0x01200000).

Upstream-Status: Pending

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
index bba981a4ca8..df894016cf0 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
@@ -306,6 +306,24 @@ gmem_stateobj_init(struct fd_screen *screen, struct gmem_key *key)
        */
       tpp_x = 6;
       tpp_y = 6;
+   } else if (is_a22x(screen)) {
+      /* a220 hardware binner: the captured webOS/KGSL driver only ever
+       * programs VSC pipes that span at most 2 bins in X (W<=2), keeping
+       * H=1 wherever the grid fits the 8 pipes.  The generic path below
+       * instead lets a single pipe span the whole row (W = nbins_x, e.g.
+       * 3 or 4 bins).  The a220 binner mis-routes primitives for such
+       * wide pipes -> garbage auto-visibility -> tile corruption and a
+       * back-end wedge on heavy scenes (e.g. glmark desktop blur).
+       *
+       * Cap pipe width at 2 bins; only grow pipe height if a tall grid
+       * cannot otherwise be covered by the 8 hardware pipes.  With w<=2
+       * the existing A2XX_VSC_PIPE_CONFIG encoding emits exactly KGSL's
+       * words (e.g. a pipe at (0,0) with w=2 -> 0x01200000). */
+      tpp_x = 2;
+      tpp_y = 1;
+      while ((DIV_ROUND_UP(gmem->nbins_y, tpp_y) *
+              DIV_ROUND_UP(gmem->nbins_x, tpp_x)) > npipes)
+         tpp_y += 1;
    } else {
       tpp_x = tpp_y = 1;
       while (DIV_ROUND_UP(gmem->nbins_y, tpp_y) > npipes)
-- 
